{
  "$schema": "/scene-schema.json",
  "id": "lru-cache",
  "title": "LRU Cache",
  "type": "lld",
  "layout": "text-left-canvas-right",
  "description": "See how an LRU Cache achieves O(1) get and put using a doubly-linked list + hashmap — the same design used in Redis and CPU cache controllers.",
  "category": "Low Level Design",
  "canvas": [
    {
      "id": "lru-list",
      "type": "linear",
      "variant": "linked-list",
      "layoutHint": "linear-H",
      "label": "Order List  (head = MRU ◀──── tail = LRU)",
      "initialState": {
        "items": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lru-map",
      "type": "map",
      "layoutHint": "hashmap-buckets",
      "label": "HashMap  key → node",
      "initialState": {
        "entries": []
      }
    }
  ],
  "activeText": {
    "initialValue": "Cache empty  (capacity = 3)"
  },
  "controls": [
    {
      "id": "btn-put1",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "put(1,'A')",
      "config": {
        "variant": "primary",
        "goToStep": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-fill",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "Fill cache (put 2,3)",
      "config": {
        "variant": "primary",
        "goToStep": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-get1",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "get(1) → HIT",
      "config": {
        "variant": "secondary",
        "goToStep": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-evict",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "put(4,'D') → Evict",
      "config": {
        "variant": "destructive",
        "goToStep": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-miss",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "get(2) → MISS",
      "config": {
        "variant": "destructive",
        "goToStep": 6
      }
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Why LinkedList + HashMap?",
        "body": "Naive: keep a list sorted by access time — but moving an element to the front is **O(n)**.\n\nSmarter: a doubly-linked list gives O(1) move-to-front when you have the node pointer. The HashMap stores `key → node`, so you find the node in O(1) first.",
        "callout": "Together: O(1) get and O(1) put. That's the whole trick."
      },
      "activeText": "put(1, 'A')  →  insert at head  [1/3]",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "value": "1→A"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A",
              "highlight": "insert"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 2",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "put(2, 'B')  →  insert at head  [2/3]",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n2",
              "value": "2→B"
            },
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "value": "1→A"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-2",
              "key": "2",
              "value": "B",
              "highlight": "insert"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 3",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "put(3, 'C')  →  CACHE FULL  [3/3]",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "value": "3→C"
            },
            {
              "id": "n2",
              "value": "2→B"
            },
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "value": "1→A"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-2",
              "key": "2",
              "value": "B"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C",
              "highlight": "insert"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Cache Hit — Move to Front",
        "body": "When `get(key)` finds the key in the HashMap:\n1. Look up the node in O(1)\n2. Detach node from current position\n3. Re-attach at head (MRU position)\n\nThis is why a **doubly**-linked list is needed — detach requires pointing to the previous node."
      },
      "activeText": "get(1)  →  CACHE HIT ✓  →  move key 1 to front",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "value": "1→A"
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "value": "3→C"
            },
            {
              "id": "n2",
              "value": "2→B"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A",
              "highlight": "hit"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-2",
              "key": "2",
              "value": "B"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Eviction — Tail is Always LRU",
        "body": "When `put(key, val)` overflows capacity:\n1. Remove the **tail node** — it's the least recently used\n2. Delete its key from the HashMap\n3. Insert new node at head\n\nO(1) because tail pointer is maintained."
      },
      "activeText": "put(4, 'D')  →  FULL! Evict LRU (key 2, tail)",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n4",
              "value": "4→D"
            },
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "value": "1→A"
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "value": "3→C"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-2",
              "key": "2",
              "value": "B (evicted)",
              "highlight": "remove"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-4",
              "key": "4",
              "value": "D",
              "highlight": "insert"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Cache Miss — Key Doesn't Exist",
        "body": "When `get(key)` doesn't find the key in the HashMap, it returns -1.\n\nThe evicted key 2 is gone from both structures — the cache has no memory of it."
      },
      "activeText": "get(2)  →  CACHE MISS ✗  →  returns -1",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n4",
              "value": "4→D"
            },
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "value": "1→A"
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "value": "3→C"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-4",
              "key": "4",
              "value": "D"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-2--get-",
              "key": "2 (get)",
              "value": "MISS → -1"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 7",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "get(3)  →  CACHE HIT ✓  →  move key 3 to front",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "value": "3→C"
            },
            {
              "id": "n4",
              "value": "4→D"
            },
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "value": "1→A"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C",
              "highlight": "hit"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-4",
              "key": "4",
              "value": "D"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 8",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "put(5, 'E')  →  FULL! Evict LRU (key 1, tail)",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n5",
              "value": "5→E"
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "value": "3→C"
            },
            {
              "id": "n4",
              "value": "4→D"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A (evicted)",
              "highlight": "remove"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-4",
              "key": "4",
              "value": "D"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-5",
              "key": "5",
              "value": "E",
              "highlight": "insert"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 9",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "get(4)  →  CACHE HIT ✓  →  move key 4 to front",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n4",
              "value": "4→D"
            },
            {
              "id": "n5",
              "value": "5→E"
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "value": "3→C"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-4",
              "key": "4",
              "value": "D",
              "highlight": "hit"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-5",
              "key": "5",
              "value": "E"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 10",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "put(1, 'A')  →  FULL! Evict LRU (key 3, tail)",
      "canvas": {
        "lru-list": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n1b",
              "value": "1→A"
            },
            {
              "id": "n4",
              "value": "4→D"
            },
            {
              "id": "n5",
              "value": "5→E"
            }
          ]
        },
        "lru-map": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "entry-1",
              "key": "1",
              "value": "A",
              "highlight": "insert"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-3",
              "key": "3",
              "value": "C (evicted)",
              "highlight": "remove"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-4",
              "key": "4",
              "value": "D"
            },
            {
              "id": "entry-5",
              "key": "5",
              "value": "E"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "popups": [
    {
      "id": "pop-head",
      "attachTo": "lru-list",
      "text": "Head = Most Recently Used",
      "showAtStep": 1,
      "hideAtStep": 2,
      "style": "info"
    },
    {
      "id": "pop-full",
      "attachTo": "lru-list",
      "text": "Cache full! Next put() will evict the tail.",
      "showAtStep": 3,
      "hideAtStep": 4,
      "style": "warning"
    },
    {
      "id": "pop-move-front",
      "attachTo": "lru-list",
      "text": "Key 1 moved to head → now MRU",
      "showAtStep": 4,
      "hideAtStep": 5,
      "style": "success"
    },
    {
      "id": "pop-evict",
      "attachTo": "lru-list",
      "text": "Key 2 (tail = LRU) evicted!",
      "showAtStep": 5,
      "hideAtStep": 6,
      "style": "warning"
    }
  ],
  "challenges": [
    {
      "id": "ch-predict-evict",
      "title": "Predict the Eviction",
      "description": "After these operations: put(1,A), put(2,B), put(3,C), get(1), put(4,D) — which key gets evicted when put(4,D) runs? Walk through each step manually to verify your answer matches the simulation.",
      "type": "predict"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-o1-proof",
      "title": "Why is it O(1)?",
      "description": "A friend says 'moving a node to the head requires scanning the list to find it — that's O(n)'. They're wrong. Explain exactly why the combination of HashMap + doubly-linked list makes both get() and put() genuinely O(1). What is each data structure responsible for?",
      "type": "optimize"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-break-lru",
      "title": "Break the Cache",
      "description": "Design a worst-case access pattern for an LRU Cache of capacity 3 where every single operation is a cache MISS. Show the sequence of put/get operations and explain why each one misses.",
      "type": "break-it"
    }
  ]
}
